    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d24-a2">

                <pb facs="0092" n="42" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg42"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 93.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hüning to Mr.
                            Gelletich.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">U.
                                S. Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1894-02-17"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">February 17,
                    1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence on the
                    matter of the arrest of John Benich, a naturalized citizen of the United States,
                    for alleged violation of the military laws of Austria-Hungary, I beg leave to
                    inform you that the U. S. minister directs me to inquire whether anything
                    further has come to your knowledge respecting his case, whether he is still in
                    Austria, or any other information which you think likely to be of interest to
                    learn.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William Hüning</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Clerk.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
